# Auth-debug scope freeze

While debugging PIN login, connection confidence, or connectivity (INT-014 class):

- **Do not** edit carousel, snap animation, transport refresh, or unrelated feature code in the same branch.
- **Do not** land large monolithic rewrites to `x02_product_shell.c` alongside auth fixes.
- Limit changes to login worker, probe guards, PIN UI, and connectivity state paths until PIN login is verified on device.

Rationale: INT-011 (~2100 lines of carousel edits) landed in the same session as INT-014 (PIN stuck on `checking...`); mixed scope makes root-cause analysis and regression attribution impossible.

When auth is verified (serial log or explicit user confirmation per `device-verify-before-done`), resume carousel/feature work on a separate branch.
